| T1  | 2024-01-15 | HARRIS TEETER #231 | Expenses:Uncategorized | 45.00  | Uncleared | none        |
# The payee is the raw NAME from the file. Tidying it is the business of
# Payees, so that this file has one job.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What a check number is worth, and for how long
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

BusinessRule A check number is trusted for a day and no longer
Description A check number is the strongest thing in a bank file: it is written
Description on the check itself, so the book and the download are naming the
Description same piece of paper. But only for as long as the number means what
Description it says. Check numbers are reused -- a new book of checks starts
Description where an old one left off, and over twenty years the same number
Description comes round again.
Details So a number settles a match only when the two are dated within the
Details book's check-number window of each other. Beyond that the number is
Details treated as coincidence and the weaker tests decide, which usually means
Details the transaction is created.
Details
Details The window is a setting on the book, a whole number of days, and it is
Details one day unless it is changed. One day is right for a book whose checks
Details are never entered before the bank reports them: nothing is outstanding,
Details so there is nothing for a number to reach back to, and a number that
Details matches anything older is more likely a number reused than a check
Details still in the post.
Details
Details At one day the number settles nothing the amount would not have settled
Details on its own, because the window on amount alone is five days and wholly
Details contains it. That is not a defect and the test is not dead: it is what
Details the setting is for. A book that records checks when they are written
Details has checks outstanding for a week or three, and widening the window is
Details what makes the number worth having. Recording a check when it is
Details written is not a thing this program does yet.
Details
Details What happens then is the point of the rule. A number that matched while
Details the dates did not is exactly the case worth seeing: either a check
Details really did take a fortnight to clear, in which case the book now holds
Details two of it and one should be deleted, or the number came round again
Details and the import was right to create one. The program cannot tell those
Details apart, so it does not try: it writes a note against the import and
Details shows the notes when the import finishes.
Details
Details Nothing is silently reconciled on a number alone, and nothing is
Details silently left out. A note that nobody reads costs a line on a screen;
Details a check quietly matched to the wrong year costs an afternoon with a
Details statement.
# Every row here is at the default window of one day.
Examples: CheckNumberWindow
| DaysApart | NumberMatches | Matched | NoteWritten | Notes                                              |
| 0         | Yes           | Yes     | No          | The number settles it                              |
| 1         | Yes           | Yes     | No          | Still within the day                               |
| 2         | Yes           | Yes     | Yes         | The number is stale, but the amount still reaches  |
| 16        | Yes           | No      | Yes         | Nothing reaches; created, and the note says why    |
| 16        | No            | No      | No          | A different number, and nothing else reaches       |

Attributes CheckNumberWindow
Description Whether a check number settles a match, by how far apart the two are
Description dated, and whether the import wrote a note about it.
Details Matched is the disposition, not the reason for it. The row two days
Details apart is matched on the amount within five days, which is the other
Details window and a weaker thing to match on -- so the note is still written,
Details because the number said one check and the dates said another and that
Details is what a person needs to see. The two windows are independent and the
Details table is where they are shown together.
| Attribute     | Type    | Default |
| DaysApart     | Integer | 0       |
| NumberMatches | Text    | Yes     |
| Matched       | Text    | No      |
| NoteWritten   | Text    | No      |
| Notes         | String  | none    |

Scenario A check number that matches too long afterwards is not matched
Description The same number sixteen days later. The number alone is not enough
Description to reconcile a check across that gap, so the transaction is created
Description and a note says what was seen -- leaving a person to decide whether
Description it is the same check or the number come round again.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                   | Type    | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking        | Bank    | false       |
| Expenses:Home:Rates    | Expense | false       |
| Expenses:Uncategorized | Expense | false       |
Given postings are : ImportedPostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Payee             | Account             | Amount   | Cleared   | CheckNo | FitId |
| T1  | 2024-01-02 | County Tax Office | Assets:Checking     | -1250.00 | Uncleared | 2041    | none  |
| T1  | 2024-01-02 | County Tax Office | Expenses:Home:Rates | 1250.00  | Uncleared | 2041    | none  |
Given import target is : ImportTarget Vertical
| AccountPath | Assets:Checking |
When transactions imported : OfxTransactions
| TrnType | DatePosted | Amount   | FitId       | Name              | Memo | CheckNum |
| CHECK   | 2024-01-18 | -1250.00 | 20240118002 | COUNTY TAX OFFICE | none | 2041     |
Then import summary is : ImportSummary Vertical
| New      | 1 |
| Matched  | 0 |
Then import notes are : ImportNote
| Kind             | Detail                                                       |
| CheckNumberStale | Check 2041 is dated 2024-01-02 here and 2024-01-18 in the file |
# The one entered by hand is untouched and uncleared; the downloaded one is a
# new transaction. The note is what tells a person to look, because only a
# person knows whether that check took a fortnight or whether the numbers came
# round again.

Attributes ImportNote
Description Something the import saw and could not decide, kept against the
Description import and shown when it finishes. Modelled on MigrationNote, which
Description does the same job for a QIF.
| Attribute | Type | Default |
| Kind      | Text |         |
| Detail    | Text |         |

