# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Resolving what the import was not sure about
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

BusinessRule A possible duplicate is the only disposition that waits
Description The other three settle themselves. A new transaction is created, a
Description duplicate is ignored, a match clears the one already there. A
Description possible duplicate is the case the program cannot settle, so it is
Description the one that asks, and nothing happens to it until it is answered.
Details There are two answers and both are ordinary. Either it is the same
Details transaction, in which case the one already in the book is the
Details transaction and the downloaded row only tells us the bank has seen it;
Details or it is a second one, in which case the bank is describing something
Details the book does not have.
Details
Details An import left unanswered changes nothing, which is what makes it safe
Details to put down and come back to. A possible duplicate quietly created
Details would double a transaction and one quietly discarded would lose it.
Details Over twenty years both happen, and the second is worse: an extra row is
Details seen and deleted, a missing one is found a year later or never.
Examples: PossibleAnswer
| Answer     | TheOneAlreadyThere                       | TheDownloadedRow            |
| TheSame    | Cleared, and stamped with the identifier | Nothing is created          |
| Different  | Nothing                                  | A transaction is created    |
| Unanswered | Nothing                                  | Nothing; it is asked again  |

Attributes PossibleAnswer
| Attribute          | Type   | Default |
| Answer             | String |         |
| TheOneAlreadyThere | String |         |
| TheDownloadedRow   | String |         |

Scenario Answering that a possible duplicate is the same transaction
Description The one already in the book is the transaction. It is cleared and
Description stamped, so the next import of the same file knows it outright
Description rather than asking again.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                   | Type    | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking        | Bank    | false       |
| Expenses:Groceries     | Expense | false       |
| Expenses:Uncategorized | Expense | false       |
Given postings are : ImportedPostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Payee         | Account            | Amount | Cleared   | FitId |
| T1  | 2026-02-05 | Harris Teeter | Assets:Checking    | -88.20 | Cleared   | none  |
| T1  | 2026-02-05 | Harris Teeter | Expenses:Groceries | 88.20  | Uncleared | none  |
Given import target is : ImportTarget Vertical
| AccountPath | Assets:Checking |
When transactions imported : OfxTransactions
| TrnType | DatePosted | Amount | FitId | Name          | Memo | CheckNum |
| DEBIT   | 2026-02-05 | -88.20 | F003  | HARRIS TEETER | none | none     |
When the possible duplicate is answered : PossibleResolution Vertical
| FitId  | F003    |
| Answer | TheSame |
Then postings are : ImportedPostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Payee         | Account            | Amount | Cleared   | FitId |
| T1  | 2026-02-05 | Harris Teeter | Assets:Checking    | -88.20 | Cleared   | F003  |
| T1  | 2026-02-05 | Harris Teeter | Expenses:Groceries | 88.20  | Uncleared | none  |
# No transaction was created. T1 now carries F003 on the posting in the account
# the statement was for, so reading the same file again reports a duplicate and
# asks nothing. The other side carries none: the bank has never heard of the
# category.

Attributes PossibleResolution
Description Which offered row is being answered, and what the answer is.
| Attribute | Type  | Default |
| FitId     | FitId |         |
| Answer    | Text  | TheSame |

Scenario Answering that a possible duplicate is a different transaction
