Scenario A row whose payee matches no account is money leaving the book
Description There is no account for it to be a transfer to, so it is not a
Description transfer and nothing is waiting: the other side is a category, like
Description any other payment to anyone the book does not keep.
Description
Description This is the common case and not a failure. Most of what leaves a
Description current account goes to somebody outside the book, and a payee that
Description matches no PaymentPayee is how that is recognised.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                   | Type       | Placeholder | PaymentPayee |
| Assets:Checking        | Bank       | false       | none         |
| Liabilities:Chase Visa | CreditCard | false       | CHASEBANK    |
| Expenses:Uncategorized | Expense    | false       | none         |
| Unassigned             | Asset      | false       | none         |
Given import target is : ImportTarget Vertical
| AccountPath | Assets:Checking |
When transactions imported : OfxTransactions
| TrnType | DatePosted | Amount  | FitId  | Name          | Memo | CheckNum |
| XFER    | 2026-04-10 | -500.00 | BNK-79 | SOME OTHER CO | none | none     |
Then postings are : ImportedPostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Payee         | Account                | Amount  | Cleared   | FitId  |
| T1  | 2026-04-10 | SOME OTHER CO | Assets:Checking        | -500.00 | Cleared   | BNK-79 |
| T1  | 2026-04-10 | SOME OTHER CO | Expenses:Uncategorized | 500.00  | Uncleared | none   |
Then balances are : AccountBalance CompareOnly
| Account    | RawBalance |
| Unassigned | 0.00       |
# Unassigned is empty, because nothing is waiting. An XFER type in the file does
# not make something a transfer: what makes it one is both halves being accounts
# this book keeps, and that is decided by the payee, not by the type.


Description Written down together because having two windows in one importer
Description invites someone to unify them, and unifying them breaks one case or
Description the other.
Examples: DateWindow
| Rule                                      | Window | Why                                   |
| A download against a transaction already entered | 5 days | A cheque takes days to clear   |
| Two new downloads proposed as one transfer | 2 days | Both halves are electronic and near  |

Attributes DateWindow
| Attribute | Type   | Default |
| Rule      | String |         |
| Window    | String |         |
| Why       | String |         |

Attributes TransferCandidateRule
| Attribute | Type    | Default |
| Test      | Integer | 0       |
| Condition | String  |         |

$WIP
Scenario A transfer between two checking accounts is proposed and approved
Description The pair observed in the two checking files in testdata: the same
Description amount out of one account and into the other on the same day.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                   | Type    | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking Prime  | Bank    | false       |
| Assets:Checking        | Bank    | false       |
| Expenses:Uncategorized | Expense | false       |
| Income:Uncategorized   | Income  | false       |
Given account mappings are : AccountMapping
| BankId    | OfxAccountId  | AccountPath           |
| 053000219 | 1023711843105 | Assets:Checking Prime |
| 053000219 | 1023711843112 | Assets:Checking       |
When statements imported : OfxImportFile
| OfxAccountId  | TrnType | DatePosted | Amount   | FitId      | Name                      |
| 1023711843105 | XFER    | 2026-07-31 | 3000.00  | 2026073101 | FROM PUGH K PRIME CHECKING |
| 1023711843112 | XFER    | 2026-07-31 | -3000.00 | 2026073102 | TO PUGH K CHECKING         |
Then transfer candidates are : TransferCandidate
| FromAccount     | FromDate   | ToAccount             | ToDate     | Amount  | DaysApart | State    |
| Assets:Checking | 2026-07-31 | Assets:Checking Prime | 2026-07-31 | 3000.00 | 0         | Proposed |
# From is the account the money left, whichever file it was read from.
When candidate approved : TransferCandidate Vertical CompareOnly
| FromAccount | Assets:Checking       |
| ToAccount   | Assets:Checking Prime |
| Amount      | 3000.00               |
Then postings are : ImportedPostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Payee                      | Account               | Amount   | Cleared | FitId      |
| T1  | 2026-07-31 | FROM PUGH K PRIME CHECKING | Assets:Checking       | -3000.00 | Cleared | 2026073102 |
| T1  | 2026-07-31 | FROM PUGH K PRIME CHECKING | Assets:Checking Prime | 3000.00  | Cleared | 2026073101 |
Then import summary is : ImportSummary Vertical
| New       | 1 |
| Duplicate | 0 |
| Matched   | 0 |
| Possible  | 0 |
# One transaction, not two, and no Uncategorized posting on either side. Each
# posting keeps the identifier of the file it came from, so re-importing
# either file recognises its own half.

Attributes OfxImportFile
Description Transactions from several files at once, each naming its account.
| Attribute    | Type        | Default    |
| OfxAccountId | Text        |            |
| TrnType      | OfxTrnType  | DEBIT      |
| DatePosted   | Date        | 2026-01-01 |
| Amount       | Money       | 0.00       |
| FitId        | FitId       |            |
| Name         | Text        | none       |
| Memo         | Text        | none       |
| CheckNum     | CheckNumber | none       |

$WIP
Scenario A credit card autopay is proposed across a two-day gap
Description The payment left the checking account on 3 August and reached the
Description card on 1 August. It is the same transfer, and this is the pair
Description that sets the window: anything narrower than three days would
Description leave it as two transactions and double the spending.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                   | Type       | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking Prime  | Bank       | false       |
| Liabilities:WF Card    | CreditCard | false       |
| Expenses:Uncategorized | Expense    | false       |
| Income:Uncategorized   | Income     | false       |
Given account mappings are : AccountMapping
| BankId    | OfxAccountId  | AccountPath           |
| 053000219 | 1023711843105 | Assets:Checking Prime |
|           | 4111111111111333 | Liabilities:WF Card |
When statements imported : OfxImportFile
| OfxAccountId     | TrnType | DatePosted | Amount   | FitId | Name                     |
| 1023711843105    | DEBIT   | 2026-08-03 | -3508.09 | C1    | WF Credit Card AUTO PAY  |
| 4111111111111333 | CREDIT  | 2026-08-01 | 3508.09  | V1    | AUTOMATIC PAYMENT THANK YOU |
Then transfer candidates are : TransferCandidate
| FromAccount           | FromDate   | ToAccount           | ToDate     | Amount  | DaysApart | State    |
| Assets:Checking Prime | 2026-08-03 | Liabilities:WF Card | 2026-08-01 | 3508.09 | 2         | Proposed |
When candidate approved : TransferCandidate Vertical CompareOnly
| FromAccount | Assets:Checking Prime |
| ToAccount   | Liabilities:WF Card   |
| Amount      | 3508.09               |
Then postings are : ImportedPostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Payee                   | Account               | Amount   | Cleared | FitId |
| T1  | 2026-08-03 | WF Credit Card AUTO PAY | Assets:Checking Prime | -3508.09 | Cleared | C1    |
| T1  | 2026-08-03 | WF Credit Card AUTO PAY | Liabilities:WF Card   | 3508.09  | Cleared | V1    |
# The date is the one from the account the money left. The card posted it two
# days earlier, and a register is kept by one date per transaction.
When report run : ReportSpec Vertical
| GroupBy  | Category   |
| From     | 2026-01-01 |
| To       | 2026-10-03 |
| Interval | Whole      |
Then report rows are : ReportRow
| Account | Level | Amount | IsSubtotal |
# No rows. Approving the pair is what keeps 3,508.09 out of the spending
# report twice over: once as an uncategorised payment from the bank and again
# as an uncategorised credit on the card.

